meta {
  name: lead capture
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/public/leads/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    // Required. First name only -- the spec is explicit that the form asks for
    // nothing else besides the email.
    "first_name": "Tess",

    // Required.
    "email": "tess@example.com",

    // Required and must be true. This is the GDPR consent checkbox
    // ("I agree to receive emails from Vida Verde"); false returns 400.
    "gdpr_consent": true,

    // Optional, defaults to "homepage". Which widget captured the lead --
    // "homepage" or "blog_post" (the same component renders under every post).
    "source": "homepage"
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  Tier 1 of the funnel: the free guide in exchange for an email.

  Sends the guide immediately and queues the nurture sequence at day 3, 7 and 14
  as `ScheduledEmail` rows. Submitting an email that is already on the list
  returns 200 without re-queueing the sequence, so a double-click cannot start a
  second run.

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Your guide is on its way. Check your inbox.",
    "id": "027dfbfa-8190-4d3b-8079-81d3be9fd24e"
  }
}
